.\"
.\" SEMOP(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SEMOP 2 "June 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
semop \- System V semaphore operations
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sem.h>
.PP
.BI "int semop(int " semid ", struct sembuf *" sops ", size_t " nsops ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR semop ()
performs operations on selected semaphores in the set indicated by
.IR semid .
Each of the
.I nsops
elements in the array
.I sops
specifies one operation:
.PP
.in +4n
.nf
struct sembuf {
    unsigned short sem_num;  /* semaphore number */
    short          sem_op;   /* semaphore operation */
    short          sem_flg;  /* operation flags */
};
.fi
.in
.PP
.I sem_flg
may be
.B IPC_NOWAIT
and/or
.BR SEM_UNDO .
The set of operations is performed
.IR atomically :
either all operations succeed at once, or none are applied and the
call blocks (or fails).
.PP
For each operation, if
.I sem_op
is:
.TP
.B positive
its value is added to the semaphore value.
.TP
.B negative
and the semaphore value is at least its absolute value, the value is
subtracted; otherwise the call blocks until it can proceed (or returns
.B EAGAIN
if
.B IPC_NOWAIT
is set).
.TP
.B zero
the call proceeds when the semaphore value is 0, otherwise it blocks
(or returns
.BR EAGAIN ).
.PP
If
.B SEM_UNDO
is set, the adjustment is recorded and automatically undone when the
process exits.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; \-1 on error with
.I errno
set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B E2BIG
.I nsops
exceeds
.BR SEMOPM .
.TP
.B EACCES
The caller lacks the required permission.
.TP
.B EAGAIN
An operation could not proceed and
.B IPC_NOWAIT
was set.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I sops
points outside the accessible address space.
.TP
.B EFBIG
A
.I sem_num
is out of range for the set.
.TP
.B EIDRM
The set was removed while the call was blocked.
.TP
.B EINTR
The call was interrupted by a signal while blocked.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I semid
is invalid, or
.I nsops
is 0.
.TP
.B ERANGE
An operation would make a semaphore value exceed
.BR SEMVMX .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR semget (2),
.BR semctl (2)
